      "dom_id": "question-98659",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the range of $f(x)=-4\\sqrt[6]{4-3x}+2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $\\sqrt[6]{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{4-3x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-4$ and then adding $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{4-3x} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -4\\sqrt[6]{4-3x} & \\le 0 \\\\ -4\\sqrt[6]{4-3x}+2 & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,2].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252721/assets/03804e230140549dd67834281d98130a0113122ded9d491b331d7ae76c621e93.png)",
