      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the range of $f(x)=-3\\sqrt[4]{2x-7}+2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The range of $\\sqrt[4]{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[4]{2x-7}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-3$ and then adding $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{2x-7} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[4]{2x-7} & \\le 0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[4]{2x-7}+2 & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,2].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252721/assets/e39c45712a29b46df780efe37214aaafb3cb7ab1fa25072c4d9ca21a8bf6c731.png)",
